
PYTHON FILE ORGANIZER

This is a file organizer that scans a directory, categorizes the files contained within, and moves them to new subdirectories based on extensions.
Can be used by anyone wanting to organize their computer!

2. Installation & Usage

How to run it: python organizer.py
Will be asked to input directory path after running...

3. Features

Categorizes files as:
- DOCUMENTS
- IMAGES
- EXECUTABLES
- ARCHIVES
- VIDEO
- AUDIO
- OTHERS

Generate human-readable text report about files categorized

4. Design Decisions
Modules:
Used pathlib because of its object oriented approach
Used glob because I couldn't get pathlib suffixes to work...
Existing files/directories handled with exist_ok=True, just leaves them as is

5. AI Tool Usage
I did not use AI tools

6. Challenges & Solutions

This was very hard! I learned a lot about python basics (lists, dictionaries, modules, creating and calling functions, error handling)
My greatest problem was getting pathlib suffixes to work for easy extension handling. I could not get it to work and researched workarounds and settled on using glob.glob